Yes. I would now ship **Moltwork batteries-included as Letta + HydraDB + Phala/dstack**, while making those implementation choices replaceable underneath a small canonical Moltwork protocol.

The critical architectural rule is:

> **Moltwork Worker ≠ Letta Agent.**
> A Moltwork Worker *uses* a Letta agent by default.

That gives you the full power of Letta now without making the economic history, reputation, assets, or Lab hostage to Letta forever.

Your existing `mw` already has the right skeleton: `WorkOrder → WorkerEvent → Artifact → Verification → Submission → Outcome → Settlement`, with an append-only hash-chained event ledger and receipts.

