# 3. Default Letta deployment

During development:

```text
LettaAgentClient({
    backend: "local"
})
```

In deployed Moltwork:

```text
LettaAgentClient({
    backend: "remote",
    url: "ws://letta-app-server:4500",
    authToken: ...
})
```

The App Server and agent execution environment live in your deployment.

Letta documents local, remote App Server and cloud as first-class backends; local runs the harness on the current machine and remote points to a user-managed App Server. ([GitHub][1])

That means the production deployment can become:

```text
PHALA / DSTACK CVM
│
├── moltwork-api
├── workerkit
├── runtime-letta
├── letta-app-server
├── hydradb
└── persistent encrypted volumes
```

and the exact same Moltwork Worker can later run against another backend.

