# 42. The architectural boundary I would put in the README

> **Moltwork is runtime-agnostic but Letta-native.**
>
> Moltwork Workers have persistent economic identities independent of their execution runtime. Letta is the reference stateful runtime and provides persistent memory, skills, subagents and continual-learning primitives. HydraDB is the reference Lab experience graph. `cg` experimentally validates changes to Workers and processes. WorkerKit records canonical execution evidence. Phala/dstack provides the reference confidential and attested deployment environment.

That's the right commitment.

Not:

> Letta is one random adapter.

You want to exploit its advanced features hard.

But also not:

> Moltwork = Letta plugin.

You want Moltwork's **experience/economic identity to outlive every framework**.

